  "body": "Refs #368\nClaim: cloud/docs-steward\nDirect-PR: one-line follow-up of the CodeRabbit round on #370, no lot\n\n## Problem\nIn #370 the capture references of a lot were restricted to open issues (so that a PR or an unknown `#N` never blocks). A capture issue closed as `not_planned` or `duplicate` then stopped blocking its lot, although the plan wants such a closure to go through human triage (`sync_state.py` treats those closures as not done).\n\n## Cause\n`known_open` filtered on `state == open`, which also drops the closed-but-not-done captures.\n\n## What changed\nKnown issue numbers (real issues, no PRs) plus the existing `not in closed` check: a PR or unknown reference still never blocks, a capture closed not planned or duplicate blocks again.\n\n## Tests\n`test_capture_closed_not_planned_or_duplicate_still_blocks_for_triage` (both reasons); the PR/unknown test of #370 still passes. Suite: 51 tests OK.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFZnKsDrPqZ8BiDUrL)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved roadmap blocker tracking so only references to real issues, other than the lot issue itself, are considered blockers. This helps prevent unrelated or invalid references from appearing as blockers.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
