st.                                                                                                                                  |\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Full details: Title check</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n**Explanation**\n\nThe title names the main behavior change: captures closed as not planned or duplicate should still block their lot. The raw summary shows a new test for the mac-labeled capture case and a change in sync_state.py's build logic that decides which referenced issues block. The title is specific and matches the changeset, so the check passes.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Full details: Docstring Coverage</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n**Explanation**\n\nDocstring coverage is 0.00% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. Docstring coverage is scoped to functions touched by this diff with cyclomatic complexity of at least 2. Documentation-only edits and deletions within surviving functions are included; unchanged diff context and fully deleted functions are excluded. Analyzed 2 functions across 2 files.\n\n**Resolution**\n\nWrite docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Finishing Touches</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>Generate docstrings</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"3e1879ae-f29b-4d0d-8e06-d12b7ba33d98\"} --> Commit to this branch\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> Create a new PR\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>Generate unit tests (beta)</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"6ba7b810-9dad-11d1-80b4-00c04fd430c8\", \"radioGroupId\": \"utg-output-choice-group-unknown_comment_id\"} --> Commit